IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `rta-types`

-- Residential Tenancies Act 1986 — GOAL 1 (PART): WORKING DAYS, SERVICE AND
-- PERIODS.
--
--   "Is a day a working day; on which day is a notice deemed given; and on
--    which day does a period of notice end?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_1986_120.txt — ss 2
-- (working day), 136, 136A.

§ `Working days, service and periods`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` n `days after` d MEANS Date (Day d PLUS n)

-- The Gregorian computus (Meeus, Jones and Butcher) for Easter Sunday; the
-- Act names Good Friday and the Tuesday after Easter without saying how
-- Easter is found.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`Easter Sunday in` y MEANS
    Date (((h PLUS l MINUS (7 TIMES m) PLUS 114) MODULO 31) PLUS 1) (FLOOR ((h PLUS l MINUS (7 TIMES m) PLUS 114) DIVIDED BY 31)) y
    WHERE
        a MEANS y MODULO 19
        b MEANS FLOOR (y DIVIDED BY 100)
        c MEANS y MODULO 100
        d MEANS FLOOR (b DIVIDED BY 4)
        e MEANS b MODULO 4
        f MEANS FLOOR ((b PLUS 8) DIVIDED BY 25)
        g MEANS FLOOR ((b MINUS f PLUS 1) DIVIDED BY 3)
        h MEANS ((19 TIMES a) PLUS b MINUS d MINUS g PLUS 15) MODULO 30
        i MEANS FLOOR (c DIVIDED BY 4)
        k MEANS c MODULO 4
        l MEANS (32 PLUS (2 TIMES e) PLUS (2 TIMES i) MINUS h MINUS k) MODULO 7
        m MEANS FLOOR ((a PLUS (11 TIMES h) PLUS (22 TIMES l)) DIVIDED BY 451)

GIVEN month IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the first Monday of month` month `in` y MEANS
    Date (1 PLUS ((8 MINUS `Weekday of` (Date 1 month y)) MODULO 7)) month y

-- s 2 "working day means any day other than— (a) a Saturday, a Sunday,
-- Waitangi Day, Anzac Day, the Sovereign's birthday, Te Rā Aro ki a
-- Matariki/Matariki Observance Day, and Labour Day; and (b) if Waitangi Day
-- or Anzac Day falls on a Saturday or a Sunday, the following Monday; and (c)
-- the day observed in the appropriate area as the anniversary of the
-- province ...; and (d) a day in the period commencing with Good Friday and
-- expiring with the Tuesday after Easter; and (e) a day in the period
-- commencing with 24 December and expiring with 3 January." The Sovereign's
-- birthday is the first Monday in June and Labour Day the fourth Monday in
-- October (Holidays Act 2003, s 44(1)).
@ref s 2 working day
@export Whether a day is a working day under s 2 of the Residential Tenancies Act 1986 (NZ): not a weekend, Waitangi Day, Anzac Day (or the Monday after either when it falls on a weekend), the Sovereign's birthday, Matariki Observance Day, Labour Day, the local anniversary day, Good Friday to the Tuesday after Easter, or 24 December to 3 January. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN d IS A DATE  @desc The day
      cal IS A `Local calendar`  @desc The Matariki Observance Days and the local anniversary days
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a working day under s 2` d cal IF
        NOT w EQUALS Saturday
    AND NOT w EQUALS Sunday
    AND NOT mondayised (Date 6 2 y)
    AND NOT mondayised (Date 25 4 y)
    AND NOT d EQUALS `the first Monday of month` 6 `in` y
    AND NOT d EQUALS `the day` 21 `days after` (`the first Monday of month` 10 `in` y)
    AND NOT elem d (cal's `Matariki Observance Days`)
    AND NOT elem d (cal's `anniversary days observed in the area`)
    AND NOT (d AT LEAST `the day` (0 MINUS 2) `days after` easter AND d AT MOST `the day` 2 `days after` easter)
    AND NOT (DATE_MONTH d EQUALS 12 AND DATE_DAY d AT LEAST 24)
    AND NOT (DATE_MONTH d EQUALS 1 AND DATE_DAY d AT MOST 3)
    WHERE
        w MEANS `Weekday of` d
        y MEANS DATE_YEAR d
        easter MEANS `Easter Sunday in` y
        GIVEN holiday IS A DATE
        GIVETH A BOOLEAN
        mondayised holiday MEANS
               d EQUALS holiday
            OR (`Weekday of` holiday EQUALS Saturday AND d EQUALS `the day` 2 `days after` holiday)
            OR (`Weekday of` holiday EQUALS Sunday AND d EQUALS `the day` 1 `days after` holiday)

-- The n-th working day after a date (n at least 1).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE, cal IS A `Local calendar`
GIVETH A DATE
`the` n `th working day after` d `, calendar` cal MEANS
    IF   n AT MOST 0
    THEN d
    ELSE IF   `is a working day under s 2` next cal
         THEN `the` (n MINUS 1) `th working day after` next `, calendar` cal
         ELSE `the` n `th working day after` next `, calendar` cal
    WHERE
        next MEANS `the day` 1 `days after` d

-- s 136 "(6) Where any document is sent by post ..., it shall be deemed, in
-- the absence of evidence to the contrary, to have been given or served on
-- the fourth working day after the date on which it was posted ... (7) ...
-- delivered to any address ... on the second working day after the date on
-- which it was delivered ... (9) If any document is transmitted to an
-- electronic address ... after 5 pm on any day, it is to be treated ... as
-- having been given or served on the next working day".
@ref s 136(6)-(9)
@export The day a notice is deemed given under s 136 of the Residential Tenancies Act 1986 (NZ): the same day if given personally or emailed by 5 pm; the 4th working day after posting; the 2nd working day after delivery to a mailbox or door; the next working day if emailed after 5 pm. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN sent IS A DATE  @desc The day the notice was given, posted, delivered or transmitted
      how IS A `Means of service`  @desc How it was served
      cal IS A `Local calendar`  @desc The Matariki Observance Days and local anniversary days
GIVETH A DATE
`the day a notice is deemed given, sent` sent `, served` how `, calendar` cal MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `personally` THEN sent
    WHEN `by post` THEN `the` 4 `th working day after` sent `, calendar` cal
    WHEN `by delivery to a mailbox or door` THEN `the` 2 `th working day after` sent `, calendar` cal
    WHEN `by email or other electronic address, by 5 pm` THEN sent
    WHEN `by email or other electronic address, after 5 pm` THEN `the` 1 `th working day after` sent `, calendar` cal

-- s 136A "the period— (a) commences on the first day after the notice is
-- given or deemed to be given under section 136; and (b) ends with the close
-- of the last day of the period." A period of n days after a notice given on
-- day G ends with the close of day G + n.
@ref s 136A
GIVEN days IS A NUMBER, given IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of a period of` days `days after notice given on` given MEANS
    `the day` days `days after` given
